                <!-- About Côte d'Ivoire Content Start -->
                <div class="why-choose-content">
                    <div class="section-title">
                        <h3 class="wow fadeInUp">About Côte d'Ivoire</h3>
                        <h2 class="text-anime-style-3" data-cursor="-opaque">Discover the Republic of Côte d'Ivoire</h2>
                        <p class="wow fadeInUp" data-wow-delay="0.2s">
                            The Republic of Côte d'Ivoire is located in West Africa along the Gulf of Guinea. It shares borders with Liberia and Guinea to the west, Mali and Burkina Faso to the north, Ghana to the east, and the Atlantic Ocean to the south. Its political capital is Yamoussoukro, while Abidjan is the country's largest city and principal economic centre.
                            <br><br>
                            Côte d'Ivoire is known for its cultural diversity, natural resources and dynamic economy. Agriculture plays an important role, with the country recognised internationally for its production of cocoa and coffee. Its economy also includes sectors such as energy, manufacturing, trade and services.
                            <br><br>
                            With its rich cultural heritage, growing economy and regional connections, Côte d'Ivoire continues to play an important role in West Africa and in international cooperation.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="why-choose-content-body">
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- About Côte d'Ivoire Content End -->
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-7">
                <!-- About Côte d'Ivoire Image Start -->
                <div class="why-choose-image-3">
